        "timestamp": 1774422832,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'The humanitarian crisis here is worsening by the minute': Israel continues to bomb Lebanon Middle East Issued on: 25/03/2026 - 08:13 More than a million people have been driven from their homes in Lebanon as Israel continues its bombardment of the country and seizes land south of the Litani River. FRANCE 24 correspondent Renée Davis reports from Beirut on the rising resentment towards Israel's ongoing air strikes. US to deploy elite army brigade to Middle East: reports 24/03/2026 Middle East Pakistan’s prime minister says his nation is ready to facilitate talks to end Iran war 24/03/2026 Middle East Saudi leader said to be pushing Trump to continue war in Iran, New York Times reports 24/03/2026 Middle East War on Iran: 'Fought on faulty assumptions, notion of externally delivered regime change delusional' 24/03/2026 Middle East Tension rises between Israel and Lebanon as IDF occupies south of Litani river 24/03/2026 Middle East Iran strikes put in question US-Israeli attacks's impact on military capabilities 24/03/2026 Middle East Inside the Palestinian camp in Beirut where residents are staying put, for now 24/03/2026 Middle East 'We do not have a single war on Iran: We have an Israeli war and an American war' 24/03/2026 Middle East Israel and US interests diverge on possible negociation for end of war 24/03/2026 Middle East"
